1
00:00:00,181 --> 00:00:07,648
Two additions to the chapter editor. One menu for every style, and three ways to see and edit the same chapter.

2
00:00:08,221 --> 00:00:13,619
A chapter is open. Every style is in one menu, each with its keyboard shortcut.

3
00:00:13,662 --> 00:00:18,739
Choose a text style and it gets a tick. The menu stays open for the next one.

4
00:00:18,804 --> 00:00:22,537
Escape goes back to the text, and what is typed has both.

5
00:00:22,580 --> 00:00:29,386
Now the same chapter as Markdown. This is not a preview. It is the chapter, and it can be edited here.

6
00:00:29,460 --> 00:00:31,742
Type a heading in Markdown.

7
00:00:31,785 --> 00:00:33,812
Switch back, and it is a heading.

8
00:00:33,887 --> 00:00:39,775
And as HTML. A script typed here is dropped, and nothing in the text is ever run.

9
00:00:40,354 --> 00:00:51,277
A test takes each example chapter through the Markdown view and the HTML view. It must come back exactly as it went in: text, styles, footnotes and images.

10
00:00:51,886 --> 00:00:59,737
The price is size. The author workspace now carries a code editor and a Markdown parser. The guide has the numbers.
